From 81c803e4461da2ce8a822f25a13f074232f0eaa7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 362/488] soh: name the 23 address-named symbols defined in
 z_en_niw.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 23 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Niw/z_en_niw.c; updating their references touches 3 files in total.

  * func_80AB5BF8 -> EnNiw_AnimateLimbs
    deduced, confidence HIGH: drives the unk_26C[] limb rotations from a
    mode argument, alternating on timer1/timer2 to flap the wings and bob
    the head

  * func_80AB6100 -> EnNiw_HopTowardTarget
    deduced, confidence HIGH: hops whenever grounded and steers world.rot.y
    toward unk_2E4 with an alternating wobble from sYawWobbleAmounts

  * func_80AB6324 -> EnNiw_WaitToFlyOff
    deduced, confidence GUESS: the params 0xD idle: does nothing until
    unk_308 is set, then launches upward; unk_308's setter is outside this
    overlay, so the trigger is inferred from the launch it performs

  * func_80AB63A8 -> EnNiw_Airborne
    deduced, confidence HIGH: holds until the cucco touches ground on the
    way down, then clears its motion state and returns to idle

  * func_80AB6450 -> EnNiw_WaitToBeLifted
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the params 4 idle: offers itself with GI_NONE
    so the player can pick it up, and reacts to being stood on

  * func_80AB6570 -> EnNiw_Idle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the default idle: offers itself to be carried,
    or starts down its path for the params 0xA river cucco

  * func_80AB6A38 -> EnNiw_FollowPath
    deduced, confidence HIGH: walks the setup path waypoint by waypoint,
    hopping toward each with EnNiw_HopTowardTarget

  * func_80AB6BF8 -> EnNiw_Held
    deduced, confidence HIGH: tumbles randomly while the player carries it
    and picks the next action on release

  * func_80AB6D08 -> EnNiw_FlutterAfterRelease
    deduced, confidence GUESS: the post-release state: flaps back to 4
    y-velocity whenever it lands and counts down the stay timer; whether
    this is gliding or hovering is not settled by the code, so the name
    records the flap-and-descend loop

  * func_80AB6EB4 -> EnNiw_FlyAway
    deduced, confidence HIGH: rises until y passes 400 and then kills the
    actor

  * func_80AB6F04 -> EnNiw_Swim
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the water state: cancels gravity, rides the
    surface spawning ripples, and bounces off walls

  * func_80AB70A0 -> EnNiw_SetupSwarmCutscene
    deduced, confidence HIGH: opens the one-point cutscene for the cucco
    swarm and starts the wind-up

  * func_80AB70A0_nocutscene -> EnNiw_SetupSwarmNoCutscene
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the port's cutscene-free variant of
    EnNiw_SetupSwarmCutscene; renamed with it so its name does not cite a
    symbol that no longer exists

  * func_80AB70F8 -> EnNiw_SwarmWindUp
    deduced, confidence HIGH: holds for the cutscene timer, then arms the
    crow that precedes the swarm

  * func_80AB714C -> EnNiw_SwarmCall
    deduced, confidence HIGH: throws the head and wings up with
    NA_SE_EV_CHICKEN_CRY_M at frame 40 and then charges the player

  * func_80AB7204 -> EnNiw_SwarmAttack
    deduced, confidence HIGH: spawns the attacking cuccos and runs at the
    player

  * func_80AB7290 -> EnNiw_SetupFlee
    deduced, confidence HIGH: restarts gCuccoAnim and installs the flee
    action at speed 4

  * func_80AB7328 -> EnNiw_Flee
    deduced, confidence HIGH: runs directly away from the player until
    timer6 expires, then resets its state

  * func_80AB7420 -> EnNiw_WaitToLand
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits for ground contact, then re-arms the hit
    counter and returns to idle

  * func_80AB747C -> EnNiw_CheckHit
    deduced, confidence HIGH: on AC_HIT decrements the hit counter, cries,
    and sends the cucco fleeing

  * D_80AB85E0 -> sCuccoSwarmActive
    deduced, confidence HIGH: overlay-wide flag set once a cucco has been
    hit enough times to summon the swarm, and cleared by the reset hook

  * D_80AB8604 -> sSwayTargets
    deduced, confidence GUESS: the two alternating targets, +/-5000, that
    unk_26C[9] approaches while the cucco stands still; the limb that field
    drives is not established

  * D_80AB860C -> sYawWobbleAmounts
    deduced, confidence HIGH: per-mode amount alternately added to and
    subtracted from the target yaw in EnNiw_HopTowardTarget

